<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Listing outcomes for two or three coins</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(cx=0)"]]A fair coin is tossed \({@n@}\) times.[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]A spinner with two equal sectors, one black and one white, is spun \({@n@}\) times.[[else]]Mutua guesses the answers to \({@n@}\) true-or-false questions. Each guess is equally likely to be right or wrong.[[/if]]</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) How many equally likely outcomes are there?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the probability that [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]there [[if test="is(j=1)"]]is exactly \({@j@}\) head[[else]]are exactly \({@j@}\) heads[[/if]][[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]the spinner lands on black exactly \({@j@}\) [[if test="is(j=1)"]]time[[else]]times[[/if]][[else]]he gets exactly \({@j@}\) right [[if test="is(j=1)"]]answer[[else]]answers[[/if]][[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the probability that [[if test="is(c=1)"]][[if test="is(cx=0)"]]there is at least one head[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]the spinner lands on black at least once[[else]]he gets at least one right answer[[/if]][[else]][[if test="is(cx=0)"]]there are no heads[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]the spinner never lands on black[[else]]he gets no right answers[[/if]][[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) List the outcomes in order ([[if test="is(cx=0)"]]H is a head and T a tail[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]B is black and W white[[else]]R is right and W wrong[[/if]]): {@ol@}. Each extra [[if test="is(cx=2)"]]question[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]spin[[else]]toss[[/if]] doubles the list, so there are \({@ta1@}\) equally likely outcomes.</p><p>(b) \({@binomial(n,j)@}\) of the outcomes in the list have [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]exactly \({@j@}\) [[if test="is(j=1)"]]head[[else]]heads[[/if]][[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]black exactly \({@j@}\) [[if test="is(j=1)"]]time[[else]]times[[/if]][[else]]exactly \({@j@}\) right [[if test="is(j=1)"]]answer[[else]]answers[[/if]][[/if]], so the probability is \(\dfrac{{@binomial(n,j)@}}{{@ta1@}} = {@ta2@}\).</p><p>(c) [[if test="is(c=1)"]]Only one outcome has none at all, so the probability of at least one is \(1 - \dfrac{1}{{@ta1@}} = {@ta3@}\).[[else]]Only one outcome in the list has none, so the probability is \(\dfrac{1}{{@ta1@}} = {@ta3@}\).[[/if]]</p><p>The number of [[if test="is(cx=0)"]]heads[[elif test="is(cx=1)"]]blacks[[else]]right answers[[/if]] can be 0 to \({@n@}\), but these \({@n+1@}\) counts are not equally likely: the counts in the middle can happen in more orders.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
