  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Probability III: listing outcomes for two or three coins</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 3.2: List the equally likely outcomes of two or three two-way experiments and find the probabilities of exactly j, at least one or none.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 19, Section B, questions B5 and B6 of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Foundation 1 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2006: coins, a spinner and guessing as contexts, randomised, with new 'at least one' and 'none' parts.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
